# SESSION-BOARD

> Inter-session board: **locks + intent + handoffs only** - never completion narrative (durable state goes to `MEMORY.md` / `project-*.md`).
> Read it at the start of any multi-session work. On every open: prune rows older than 3 days (verify first - an old row is suspect, not a lock). Budget <= 6 KB (HANDOFF QUEUE not counted).
> Rules: global AGENTS.md, Inter-session coordination. Rationale: docs/03-inter-session.md.
> Every example row below is fictional - delete it once you have read it.

## IN-FLIGHT

Work in progress on a shared resource = a lock. Add the row BEFORE you start; delete it the moment you finish. Another session's row = do not touch that resource (leave a MESSAGE instead).

| owner (session) | since | resource / work | worktree / branch |
|---|---|---|---|
| web-session | 2026-01-15 | acme-erp: invoice status migration | ../acme-erp-invoice / feat/invoice-status |

## RESERVATIONS

Collidable identifiers (migration timestamps, branch names) taken before use. Take NEXT FREE, then bump it.

- NEXT FREE migration timestamp: 20260115120100
- 20260115120000 - web-session - add_invoice_status (2026-01-15)

## DEPLOY LOCK

One rebuild of a shared container/host at a time. ACTIVE empty -> put yourself there and deploy; ACTIVE taken -> add yourself to WAITING and do not deploy. ACTIVE pulls the latest default branch before building (piggyback: a WAITING entry whose commit is already in that image deletes itself). Delete ACTIVE as soon as the health check passes; ACTIVE older than 15 min -> verify container status before stealing. Migrations use RESERVATIONS, not this lock.

- ACTIVE: web-session 2026-01-15 14:05 UTC - acme-erp frontend @ abc1234
- WAITING: (none)

## HANDOFF QUEUE

Facts this session changed in a file it does not own - one line each, written BEFORE deleting your IN-FLIGHT row. A fact sentence, not a resource label. Folded only by `memory-save` of the target file, and deleted in that same edit (delete-iff-folded). Exempt from the 3-day prune and the budget; entries older than 14 days -> flag to the user.

-> project-acme-erp.md :: migration add_invoice_status applied on prod; the old status column was dropped  [from web-session 2026-01-15]

## CONTRACTS

Interface agreements between sessions (shared schema, API shapes, event names) that both sides build against.

- acme-erp `invoices.status` = draft | issued | paid | void - agreed by web-session + erp-session (2026-01-15)

## MESSAGES

Notes for another session - use instead of touching a resource it has locked.

